    "q-44709": {
      "dom_id": "step-q44709",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following polynomials **IS NOT** written in standard form?",
      "worked_solution": "A polynomial is written in standard form when the terms are arranged in descending order of the variable's exponent. The first term should have the largest exponent, and the last term should have the smallest exponent.\n\nThe polynomial \n\n$$\n1-x-5{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis *not* in standard form. The highest exponent term is $-5{x}^{2},$ followed by $-x,$ and finally $1.$ So, the standard form is \n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}-x+1\n$$\n\nwhich is different from the given arrangement.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
