    "q-217281": {
      "dom_id": "step-q217281",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Express the polynomial $1-2{b}^{4}+{b}^{3}+5{b}^{2}$ in standard form.\n\n$1-2{b}^{4}+{b}^{3}+5{b}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To write a polynomial in **standard form**, we must arrange the terms in descending order of the variable's exponent. The first term should have the largest exponent, and the last term should have the smallest exponent.\n\nThe highest exponent term is $-2{b}^{4},$ followed by ${b}^{3},$ and then $5{b}^{2},$ and finally $1.$\n\nSo, the standard form of the polynomial is\n\n$$\n-2{b}^{4}+{b}^{3}+5{b}^{2}+1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
