    "q-110820": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110820",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The standard form of the polynomial $3{c}^{2}-5{c}^{2}-6{c}^{4}+7$ is",
      "worked_solution": "First, we collect like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{c}^{2}-5{c}^{2}-6{c}^{4}+7 & = \\\\ (3{c}^{2}-5{c}^{2})-6{c}^{4}+7 & = \\\\ (3-5){c}^{2}-6{c}^{4}+7 & = \\\\ -2{c}^{2}-6{c}^{4}+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to express our polynomial in standard form.\n\nThe highest exponent term is $-6{c}^{4},$ followed by $-2{c}^{2},$ and finally $7.$\n\nSo, the standard form of the polynomial is:\n\n$$\n-6{c}^{4}-2{c}^{2}+7\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
